                y = 0.242,
                step = 5,
                label = "Freka Bloodaxe - Horde example vendor",
                mapName = "Icecrown",
            },
        },
        itemId = 45725,
        name = "Argent Hippogryph",
        mountCategory = "Vendor",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete the tournament training and one city's championship, then farm Champion's Seals.\n\n1. Start The Argent Tournament with Justicar Mariel Trueheart in Icecrown (69.6, 22.8). Finish the combat lessons, collect 15 Aspirant's Seals from the daily training, and win The Aspirant's Challenge.\n\n2. Complete your first city's Valiant training: collect 25 Valiant's Seals through its dailies, win The Valiant's Challenge, and turn in A Champion Rises. This unlocks that city's quartermaster and Champion's Seal activities.\n\n3. Finish Crusader Rhydalla's investigation through The Black Knight's Fall to unlock Threat From Above. Keep doing the Champion dailies and open any Champion's Purses you select as rewards.\n\n4. Add a daily Heroic Trial of the Champion clear at the Coliseum's five-player entrance (75.1, 21.8). Loot all bosses. Keep saving until the currency panel shows 150 Champion's Seals.\n\n5. Buy Argent Hippogryph from your unlocked city quartermaster. For example, Champion of Stormwind can use Corporal Arthur Flew in the Alliance pavilion (76.4, 19.2); Champion of Orgrimmar can use Freka Bloodaxe in the Horde pavilion (76.4, 24.2). Use the item to learn the mount.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=45725",
        difficultyReason = "Complete the tournament training and one city's championship, then farm Champion's Seals.",
        difficulty = "medium",
    },
    [63956] = {
        category = "Achievements",
        source = "Glory of the Ulduar Raider - current merged achievement",
        tips = "The current meta awards both Rusted and Ironbound. Use achievement 12401, not the retired separate 10/25-player metas. Plan controlled damage before Razorscale and XT; accidental kills consume that week's attempt.",
        sourceComments = { 2547651, 2545906, 2557992, 6054277, 2860394 },
        waypoints = {
            {
                mapID = 120,
                x = 0.41600000000000004,
                y = 0.182,
                step = 1,
                label = "Ulduar raid entrance - current merged meta",
                mapName = "The Storm Peaks",
            },
        },
        itemId = 45801,
        name = "Ironbound Proto-Drake",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 11,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Complete the current unified Ulduar challenge meta; several mechanics need deliberate setup and repeat lockouts.\n\n1. Track Glory of the Ulduar Raider (12401). Enter the normal legacy Ulduar raid at 41.6, 18.2 in the Storm Peaks. Before pulling, remove damage-proc equipment, dismiss attacking pets, and arrange a low-damage option such as Whole-Body Shrinka' for the delicate encounters.\n\n2. Flame Leviathan - Orbit-uary: talk to the Lore Keeper of Norgannon at the entrance to activate the orbital defenses, leave all four defense towers intact, then kill Leviathan. Starting the ordinary assault without the defense systems is not the required hard mode.\n\n3. Razorscale - Iron Dwarf, Medium Rare: keep Dark Rune Guardian dwarves alive. Let the engineers finish the launchers, wait for Razorscale's berserk to strengthen her breath, then harpoon her down and position the Guardians in front of her. Let her breath kill 25 Guardians. Reduce her below half only with controlled damage if you want her permanently grounded. Track the dwarf counter; if short, reset without killing her and continue, since the counter can accumulate across attempts.\n\n4. Ignis - Stokin' the Furnace: kill him within four minutes. XT-002 - Heartbreaker: carefully lower XT to about 75%, stop attacking the body as the heart emerges, destroy the exposed heart on that first phase, then kill the restored hard-mode boss. A one-shot on XT bypasses the heart and fails the criterion.\n\n5. Assembly of Iron - I Choose You, Steelbreaker: kill Runemaster Molgeim and Stormcaller Brundir before Steelbreaker. Kologarn - Disarmed: destroy both arms, then finish the body within 12 seconds. Auriaya - Crazy Cat Lady: kill Auriaya with single-target damage while her Sanctum Sentries remain alive.\n\n6. Hodir - I Could Say That This Cache Was Rare: defeat him quickly enough to preserve the rare cache. Thorim - Lose Your Illusion: start the arena event, clear its opening, operate the gauntlet access, and reach Thorim before Sif leaves, then defeat him with Sif present. Do not wait out the hard-mode timer.\n\n7. Freya - Knock, Knock, Knock on Wood: leave all three named Elders alive before engaging Freya, then complete the encounter. Clearing the Elder mini-bosses for convenience disables this criterion.\n\n8. Mimiron - Firefighter: press the big red button before beginning the fight to enable Self-Destruct. Defeat each phase, then disable the three combined machine sections close together so they cannot repair one another. The ordinary Mimiron kill does not count.\n\n9. General Vezax - I Love the Smell of Saronite in the Morning: keep Vezax alive and do not kill any Saronite Vapors. Wait for all eight to combine into the Saronite Animus. Kill the Animus first, then Vezax. Killing a vapor can prevent the required Animus from spawning.\n\n10. Yogg-Saron - One Light in the Darkness: use at most one Keeper's assistance. Zero is also valid and preserves a Mimiron's Head chance. Kill Guardians beside Sara, enter brain portals, clear the illusion and damage the brain before Induce Madness, then exit and finish Yogg without exhausting Sanity.\n\n11. Check the tracked meta for any failed encounter before ending the run. Return on a later weekly lockout for a boss killed with its condition unmet. When the current meta completes, check the journal and mailbox for both proto-drakes and learn any reins received; there is no second 25-player meta to grind.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=45801",
        difficultyReason = "Complete the current unified Ulduar challenge meta; several mechanics need deliberate setup and repeat lockouts.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
